From ubbb9357156c132fe at groups.google.com  Wed Mar  6 14:21:15 2013
From: ubbb9357156c132fe at groups.google.com (Daniel Simpson)
Date: Wed, 06 Mar 2013 14:21:15 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] Large Bivariate Spatial Model
Message-ID: <p1BYEhoM6VI.OnAOVQ9fB5cJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <p1BYEhoM6VI.jJf57Vxrpi0J@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <p1BYEhoM6VI.8IIAOQ4hqtkJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com> <p1BYEhoM6VI.jJf57Vxrpi0J@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/p1BYEhoM6VI/m/OnAOVQ9fB5cJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It can estimate the cross-covariance.  The general form is

y_1 ~ b_{11} f_1 + b_{12} f_2
y_2 ~ b_{21} f_1 + b_{22} f_2
where b_{21} = b_{12} is (related  to) the cross covariance.

(here f_1 and f_2 are independent Gaussian random fields, possibly
with different parameters)

D

