Dear Finn,

Thanks a lot for your feedback. I went for the solution below. It's a
pitty that the replicate argument does not takes factors.

inla(y ~ factor(month) + f(year, model = "rw1", replicate = location) +
f(location, model = "iid"), family = "poisson", data = dataset,

control.predictor = list(compute = TRUE, link = link))

Best regards,

Thierry

Op 08-03-13 11:12, Finn Lindgren schreef:

> On 08/03/13 10:00, thierry....@gmail.com wrote:
>> Dear all,
>>
>> We have a dataset spanning about 20 years with data from about 1000
>> locations. Each location is sampled 6 times per year. A randow walk
>> along year per location would be a good thing for this dataset. We
>> sloved this by creating a new vector year2 = location * (nYear + 200)
>> + year. So year2 looks like 1:20 for location 0,  201:220 for
>> location 1, 401:420 for location 2, ... Then we added a f(year2,
>> model = 'rw1') component to the model. Is this OK or is it rubbish?
>> The example below seems to give reasonable results. Though the year2
>> effects seems to have some positive bias.
>
> Hi, it should be a rough approximation of independent realisations for
> each location, since you have relatively long gaps in between the
> segments you use, but the correct way to do that is to use "replicate"
> in the f() specifications, and use 1:20 for every location in "year2".
> That will also reduce the size of your model drastically.
>
> Finn
>
>>
>> Best regards,
>>
>> Thierry
>>
>> library(INLA)
>> library(ggplot2)
>> set.seed(12345)
>> nLocation <- 20
>> nYear <- 20
>> nMonth <- 6
>> Intercept <- 3
>> Season <- 2
>> sdYear <- 0.1
>> sdTrend <- 0.05
>> sdLocation <- 3
>> rho <- 0.5
>> burnin <- 50
>> probMissing <- 0.2
>>
>> dataset <- expand.grid(year = seq_len(nYear), month =
>> seq_len(nMonth), location = seq_len(nLocation))
>> dataset$Fixed <- Intercept + Season * cos(pi * (dataset$month -
>> round(mean(dataset$month))) / nMonth)
>> Random <- matrix(rnorm(nLocation, mean = 0, sd = sdLocation), ncol =
>> nYear + burnin, nrow = nLocation)
>>
>> Error <- matrix(rnorm((nYear + burnin) * nLocation, mean = 0, sd =
>> sdYear), ncol = nYear + burnin)
>> for(i in tail(seq_len(nYear + burnin), -1)){
>>   Random[, i] <- rho * Random[, i - 1] + Error[, i]
>> }
>> Random <- Random[, -seq_len(burnin)]
>> dataset$Random <- apply(dataset[, c("location", "year")], 1,
>> function(x){
>>   Random[x["location"], x["year"]]
>> })
>> dataset$Random <- dataset$Random + rnorm(nLocation, mean = 0, sd =
>> sdTrend)[dataset$location] * dataset$year
>> dataset$y <- rpois(nrow(dataset), lambda = exp(dataset$Fixed +
>> dataset$Random))
>> dataset$y0 <- dataset$y
>> dataset$y[rbinom(nrow(dataset), prob = probMissing, size = 1) == 1]
>> <- NA
>> ggplot(subset(dataset, !is.na <http://is.na>(y)), aes(x = year, y = location)) +
>> geom_point() + facet_wrap(~month)
>> ggplot(dataset, aes(x = year, y = y0, colour = factor(month))) +
>> geom_line() + facet_wrap(~location, scales = "free_y")
>>
>>
>> dataset$year2 <- with(dataset, location * (nYear + 200) + year)
>> link <- rep(NA, nrow(dataset))
>> link[is.na <http://is.na>(dataset$y)] <- 1
>> model3 <- inla(y ~ factor(month) + f(year2, model = "rw1"), family =
>> "poisson", data = dataset, control.predictor = list(compute = TRUE,
>> link = link))
>> plot(model3)
>> test <- merge(dataset, model3$summary.random$year2, by.x = "year2",
>> by.y = "ID")
>> colnames(test)[11:13] <- c("LCL", "Median", "UCL")
>> ggplot(test, aes(x = year, y = Random)) + geom_ribbon(aes(ymin = LCL,
>> ymax = UCL), alpha = 0.1, fill = "blue") + geom_line(aes(y = mean),
>> colour = "blue") + geom_line() + facet_wrap(~location, scales =
>> "free_y")
>>
